<p class="lt-chem-36557">Sample W is a reactant for a wide range of biochemical processes. Sample X was isolated from vanilla beans. Elemental analysis indicated the compounds are structural isomers with the composition: 54.52% C, 9.16% H and 36.32% O. The IR spectrum for each compound showed a broad absorption from 3500 - 2500 cm<sup>-1</sup> and a strong band near 1710 cm<sup>-1</sup>. The <sup>1</sup>H NMR is being serviced, so only the <sup>13</sup>C NMR spectra shown below were available.</p>

